('cleghorn-2n47','Cleghorn Fire Road (2N47)','Cajon Pass / San Bernardino','Beginner','Ridge run with incredible views. The main road is 2WD friendly; offshoots require 4x4. Perfect introduction to mountain wheeling with panoramic vistas of the Cajon Pass.','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1464822759023-fed622ff2c3b?w=800&q=80',34.3031,-117.4524),
('lytle-creek','Lytle Creek / Stockton Flats','Lytle Creek, CA','Beginner','Perfect for a quick run. Light water crossings and shaded campsites along the creek. Great for families and beginner groups looking to practice water crossing techniques.','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1494522855154-9297ac14b55f?w=800&q=80',34.2583,-117.5025),
('holcomb-creek','Holcomb Creek','Big Bear / Holcomb Valley','Advanced','Iconic rock crawling trail. The Gatekeeper sets the tone - if you can''t clear it, turn back. Holcomb Creek crossing and deep ruts make this a must-do for experienced wheelers.','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1464822759023-fed622ff2c3b?w=800&q=80',34.2578,-117.0894),
('gold-mountain','Gold Mountain (3N69)','Big Bear / Baldwin Lake','Advanced','Starts easy, ends challenging. The rock garden at the summit tests both driver and rig. Nylon strap recommended - this trail is notorious for body damage. Unmatched summit views of Baldwin Lake.','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1441974231531-c6227db76b6e?w=800&q=80',34.2722,-116.8247),
('dishpan-springs','Dishpan Springs','Big Bear Lake','Extreme','The big leagues. Deep bowls, off-camber climbs, and shelf roads that''ll test the best-built rigs. Named for the bathtub-size springs. Bring recovery gear and expect body damage.','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1469854523086-cc02fe5d8800?w=800&q=80',34.2347,-117.0469),
('mojave-road-west','Mojave Road (West/Central)','Mojave National Preserve','Beginner','Historic desert crossing from Colorado River to Barstow. Sand, lava tubes, volcanic formations, and the iconic Mojave mailbox. Bring extra fuel and water.','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1486870591958-9b9d0d1dda99?w=800&q=80',35.1489,-115.9033),
('ocotillo-wells','Ocotillo Wells SVRA','Ocotillo Wells, CA','Moderate','California''s largest OHV area. Sand dunes, badlands, mud caves, and slot canyons. Blowsand Hill tests your climbing skills.','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1472396961693-142e6e269027?w=800&q=80',33.1439,-116.1347),
